description:
Org-unit aggregation workflow that exports CHAP-ready wide CSV. Loads a published GeoZarr dataset over a time range, spatially aggregates its variable(s) within each GeoJSON feature (e.g. a DHIS2 organisation unit) using the chosen method, and writes one row per location-period with columns `time_period`, `location`, and one column per variable.

Each feature's GeoJSON `id` becomes the `location`, each time step becomes `time_period` (formatted according to `period_type`). Aggregation is at the dataset's native temporal resolution, so set `period_type` to match it (e.g. `month` for a monthly dataset). This is the same pipeline as `aggregate_to_dhis2_json` but emits CHAP CSV instead of DHIS2 JSON.

Usage — call this process as the result of a process graph:

{
  "agg": {
    "process_id": "aggregate_to_chap_csv",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "era5land_precipitation_monthly",
      "temporal_extent": ["2025-01-01", "2025-12-31"],
      "geometries": { "type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [ ... ] },
      "method": "mean",
      "period_type": "month"
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
